From: Stephender (Antigravity Phase 3, Fix 6 replacement — render-worker priority)
Subject: [PATCH] Lower Cycles CPU render worker thread OS priority during renders

Phase 3 Fix 6 replacement (supersedes the rejected tile-size Fix 6 from Job #12
and the rejected 3-core cap from Job #14). Applies cleanly on top of
0001-undo-hardening + 0002-physical-ram + 0003-ram-aware-cache +
0004-tbb-trim-thp-guard + 0005-startup-ram-lazy-loading + 0006-packaging-trim
against Blender v5.2.4 (cd5dc428cce1).

Motivation (Job #14 measurements on 4-vCPU Linux VM, BMW27 64-sample CPU):
- Lowering render OS priority to nice +10 cut foreground probe latency by -47.4%
  pooled median (178.96 -> 94.20 ms), -46.8% p95 (206.54 -> 109.91 ms), and
  -59.8% quiet worst-case (273.96 -> 110.03 ms), for +0.46% render time on a
  clean run (+1.77% 2-run mean), with all 4 threads preserved and pixel-identical
  807,001-byte output (0 / 518,400 differing pixels).

Design summary
--------------
1. intern/cycles/util/thread_priority.h (new header, registered in
   intern/cycles/util/CMakeLists.txt) + intern/cycles/util/thread.cpp:
   - Adds `ccl::ScopedLowThreadPriority`, an RAII guard that lowers ONLY the
     calling thread's OS scheduling priority while in scope and restores it on
     scope exit where permitted by the OS:
     * Windows (_WIN32): `GetThreadPriority` / `SetThreadPriority` to
       `THREAD_PRIORITY_BELOW_NORMAL`, restored unconditionally on exit. Does
       not use `THREAD_MODE_BACKGROUND_BEGIN` (avoids I/O & memory-page
       throttling on 8 GB systems) or `THREAD_PRIORITY_IDLE` (avoids starvation).
     * Linux (__linux__): per-thread `getpriority`/`setpriority(PRIO_PROCESS,
       syscall(SYS_gettid), 10)` targeting only the calling kernel thread (LWP),
       with `errno` preserved and best-effort restore on exit (succeeds under
       `CAP_SYS_NICE`/`RLIMIT_NICE`; silently no-ops with `EACCES` for
       unprivileged users while keeping the main/UI thread at nice 0).
     * Other platforms: no-op default ctor/dtor.
   - Strictly monotonic: never raises a thread that is already running at an
     equal or lower priority (e.g., user-launched `nice -n 15` or Windows
     `THREAD_PRIORITY_LOWEST`/`IDLE`).
   - Placed in a dedicated header (`util/thread_priority.h`) included only by
     `util/thread.cpp` and `integrator/path_trace_work_cpu.cpp` to avoid
     invalidating ccache/sccache across the rest of Cycles.
   - No BLI OS thread-priority helper exists in Blender v5.2.4, and Cycles util
     is standalone (no BLI dependency).

2. intern/cycles/integrator/path_trace_work_cpu.cpp:
   - Converts the CPU compute `parallel_for` loops (`render_samples`,
     `adaptive_sampling_converge_filter_count_active`, `cryptomatte_postproces`,
     and `denoise_volume_guiding_buffers`) to `blocked_range` chunks and places
     `const ScopedLowThreadPriority low_priority;` at the start of each chunk
     (identical oneTBB grainsize=1 / auto_partitioner load balancing; ~tens of
     chunks per batch instead of per-pixel syscalls).
   - Covers every thread that executes Cycles CPU render work inside
     `local_arena` (`Session::session_thread_` in slot 0 and the `N-1` oneTBB
     pool workers in slots 1..N-1), while NEVER touching Blender's main/UI
     thread, `WM_jobs` render job thread, GPU path tracing (`PathTraceWorkGPU`),
     EEVEE/Workbench, depsgraph, or compositor.
   - Intentionally leaves `PathTraceWorkCPU::copy_to_display()` at normal
     priority so no display/GPU texture-mapping lock is held at lowered priority.
   - Default-on with no new user preference or UI change.

Verification performed on this Linux machine
--------------------------------------------
- Full 7-patch stack (0001..0006 + this patch) verified to apply cleanly on
  Blender v5.2.4 (cd5dc428cce1) in a clean scratch clone.
- `intern/cycles/util/thread.cpp` + `thread_priority.h` compiled with
  `g++ -std=c++20 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -Wshadow -Wconversion`:
  * Linux native build + live `/proc/<pid>/task/*/stat` test confirmed:
    main thread nice=0, non-render thread nice=0, 3 worker threads nice=10,
    pre-niced thread nice=15 (not raised), `errno` preserved.
  * Mock `_WIN32` build + unit test confirmed lowering to BELOW_NORMAL,
    symmetric restore to NORMAL, and monotonicity for LOWEST/ERROR_RETURN.
  * Non-Linux/non-Windows `#else` branch compiled cleanly with zero warnings.
- NOT YET VERIFIED (requires CI + Windows desktop): full Blender Linux/Windows
  CMake build and link, `path_trace_work_cpu.cpp` compilation against full
  Cycles headers, post-CI Linux live Cycles render `/proc` & BMW27 timing/PNG
  re-check, and real Windows desktop interactive responsiveness + bare-metal
  render-time check.

